{%- comment -%}
  past-pieces-gallery — the Gallery page's card mosaic. 1 use:
  page.past-pieces, which is the page handle `jewellery-gallery`.

  PORTED FROM AN FYE-ORIGINAL, NOT FROM T4S. The old file was already written
  to the brand book, so this is a re-plumbing rather than a redesign. Kept
  exactly: the card anatomy (monogram + name + category, square media
  carousel, caption, spec line), the ordering rule, and the masonry mechanic.
  Changed: palette and type now come from fye-core.css tokens, `{% style %}`
  became `{% stylesheet %}`, and the inline <script> moved to
  assets/fye-ui.js.

  DROPPED FROM THE OLD SCHEMA — settings a schema no longer declares are
  ignored by Shopify, so nothing saved in the theme editor is lost:
    load_fonts                        layout/theme.liquid loads both faces
    padding_top, padding_top_mobile   rhythm is --sect-y via .band
    enquire_label, default_enquire_url  the card footer that used them was
                                      removed by Ed on 25/08/2026
  GAINED: bg_color, a palette choice, replacing a hard-coded ivory ground.

  WHERE THE CONTENT COMES FROM
  One `past_piece` METAOBJECT per commission — Content > Metaobjects > Past
  Piece. Nothing about a piece is edited in the theme editor; this section
  carries layout and labels only. Fields read here: name, category, label,
  media, caption, spec, date, featured.

  `number` is deliberately NOT rendered (Ed, 25/08/2026), and neither is the
  date. Both fields still exist and must not be deleted — the date orders the
  grid, the number is an internal reference.

  Order is automatic: featured pieces first, then newest by date completed.
  Nothing is dragged into place.

  Categories come from the entry's Category field. To add one, add it to the
  metaobject definition AND to `cat_order` below — the bar renders in that
  order and hides categories with no pieces. Present at 01/09/2026:
  Engagement, Wedding, Pendants.

  KNOWN LIMIT (W514): a Liquid loop over `.values` reads at most 50 entries.
  11 exist today, so the ceiling is years out, but past it the OLDEST pieces
  vanish silently rather than erroring. The fix is wrapping the grid in a
  paginate tag, which also moves the filter counts server-side.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.bg_color | default: 'ivory'
  assign initial = s.items_initial | plus: 0

  assign pieces = metaobjects.past_piece.values
  assign piece_count = pieces.size

  comment
    Sort key per entry: featured flag, then date, then the entry's position,
    sorted descending — so featured pins to the top and the rest run newest
    first.

    The position travels IN the key and the entry is found by walking the list
    again below. That looks wasteful and is: `.values` is a collection drop
    that supports iteration only. values[i] returns nil, which renders a card
    with every field empty and raises nothing at all. Do NOT "optimise" this
    into an index lookup. Handles are no good either —
    metaobjects.TYPE[handle] is capped at 20 lookups per page.
  endcomment
  assign sort_keys = ''
  for p in pieces
    assign pin = '0'
    if p.featured.value
      assign pin = '1'
    endif
    assign d = p.date.value | default: '0000-00-00' | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
    assign sort_keys = sort_keys | append: pin | append: d | append: '~' | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
  endfor
  assign ordered = sort_keys | split: ',' | sort | reverse

  assign cat_order = 'Engagement,Wedding,Eternity Rings,Gemstone,Pendants,Earrings,Bracelets' | split: ','
  assign present = ''
  for p in pieces
    assign c = p.category.value
    unless present contains c
      assign present = present | append: c | append: ','
    endunless
  endfor
  assign distinct_count = present | split: ',' | size

  assign show_bar = false
  if s.show_filters and distinct_count > 1
    assign show_bar = true
  endif
-%}

<section class="ppg band band--{{ band }}" data-screen-label="Gallery — past pieces" data-fye-gallery>
  <div class="wrap">

    {%- if show_bar -%}
      <nav class="ppg__filters" data-fye-gallery-filters aria-label="Filter pieces by category">
        <button class="ppg__filter is-on" type="button" data-fye-gallery-filter="all">
          {{ s.all_label | default: 'All pieces' }}
          <span class="ppg__tally" data-fye-gallery-tally aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        {%- for cat in cat_order -%}
          {%- if present contains cat -%}
            <button class="ppg__filter" type="button" data-fye-gallery-filter="{{ cat | handleize }}">
              {{ cat }}
              <span class="ppg__tally" data-fye-gallery-tally aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if piece_count == 0 -%}
      <p class="lead">No pieces yet. Add one at Content &rsaquo; Metaobjects &rsaquo; Past Piece.</p>
    {%- else -%}

      <div class="ppg__grid" data-fye-gallery-grid>
        {%- for key in ordered -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign card_index = forloop.index
            assign pi = key | split: '~' | last | plus: 0
            assign piece = nil
            for p in pieces
              if forloop.index0 == pi
                assign piece = p
                break
              endif
            endfor
          -%}
          {%- if piece == nil -%}{% continue %}{%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign piece_title = piece.name.value | default: 'Untitled piece'
            assign cat_label = piece.category.value
            assign media = piece.media.value
            comment
              `| default: 0` so an empty media field is 0 rather than nil: nil
              fails BOTH the "> 1" and the "== 0" test, and the card then
              renders with no carousel and no placeholder — an empty box.
            endcomment
            assign total = media.size | default: 0
          -%}

          <article class="ppg__card{% if card_index > initial %} is-capped{% endif %}" data-cat="{{ cat_label | handleize }}">

            <div class="ppg__head">
              <span class="ppg__mono">
                {%- if s.avatar != blank -%}
                  {{ s.avatar | image_url: width: 76 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '' }}
                {%- else -%}
                  <img src="{{ 'fye-icon-teal.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="19" height="26" loading="lazy">
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="ppg__who">
                <span class="ppg__name">{{ piece_title }}</span>
                <span class="ppg__meta">
                  {{- cat_label -}}
                  {%- if piece.label.value != blank %} &middot; {{ piece.label.value }}{% endif -%}
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="ppg__car"{% if total > 1 %} data-fye-car{% endif %}>
              {%- if total > 1 -%}
                <span class="ppg__count" data-fye-car-count>1 / {{ total }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}

              <div class="ppg__track" data-fye-car-track>
                {%- if total == 0 -%}
                  <div class="ppg__slide ppg__ph">
                    <span class="ppg__ph-note">No photographs on this piece yet</span>
                  </div>
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- for item in media -%}
                    {%- if item.media_type == 'video' -%}
                      <div class="ppg__slide">
                        <span class="ppg__vtag">{% render 'icon', name: 'play', size: 12 %}Video</span>
                        {%- comment -%}
                          image_size sets the POSTER resolution. Without it
                          Shopify serves a small thumbnail, scaled up to fill a
                          square card, and the first frame looks badly blurred
                          until the viewer presses play. 1080 is the largest
                          width this grid ever requests.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        {{ item | video_tag: image_size: '1080x', playsinline: true, muted: true, controls: true, preload: 'metadata' }}
                      </div>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- assign img_alt = item.alt | default: piece_title -%}
                      <div class="ppg__slide">
                        {{ item | image_url: width: 1080 | image_tag:
                           loading: 'lazy',
                           widths: '420, 640, 840, 1080',
                           sizes: '(max-width: 560px) 100vw, (max-width: 900px) 50vw, 420px',
                           alt: img_alt }}
                      </div>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              {%- if total > 1 -%}
                <button class="ppg__arrow ppg__arrow--prev" type="button" data-fye-car-prev aria-label="Previous photograph">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-left', size: 16 -%}
                </button>
                <button class="ppg__arrow ppg__arrow--next" type="button" data-fye-car-next aria-label="Next photograph">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-right', size: 16 -%}
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- if total > 1 -%}
              <div class="ppg__dashes" data-fye-car-dashes aria-hidden="true">
                {%- for slot in (1..total) -%}
                  <span class="ppg__dash{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"></span>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Rich text MUST go through metafield_tag. Both obvious alternatives
              print the raw structure onto the page instead of rendering it, and
              neither raises an error:
                {{ piece.caption.value }} -> {"type"=>"root", "children"=>[...]}
                {{ piece.caption }}       -> {"type":"root","children":[...]}
              metafield_tag wraps its output in div.metafield-rich_text_field,
              which is why the caption rules below target descendants.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if piece.caption != blank -%}
              <div class="ppg__caption">{{ piece.caption | metafield_tag }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if piece.spec.value != blank -%}
              <p class="ppg__spec">{{ piece.spec.value }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

          </article>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- if piece_count > initial -%}
        <div class="ppg__more" data-fye-gallery-more-wrap>
          <button class="btn btn--outline" type="button" data-fye-gallery-more>
            {{ s.more_label | default: 'Load more pieces' }}
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---- filter bar --------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .ppg__filters {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--s3) var(--s7);
  margin-bottom: var(--s9);
}
.fye .ppg__filter {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s1);
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0 0 var(--s1);
  border: 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  background: none;
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease), border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .ppg__filter:hover { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .ppg__filter.is-on { color: var(--ink); border-bottom-color: var(--line-strong); }
.fye .ppg__tally { opacity: 0.6; }

/* ---- the mosaic --------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Default is an even grid, which is what a visitor without JavaScript gets and
   is perfectly readable. fye-ui.js adds .is-masonry, switching the rows to 1px
   tracks and giving each card a row span matching its measured height.

   Why not CSS columns: they balance by HEIGHT, which puts card 3 of 3 on the
   second row and makes cards read DOWN each column instead of across — wrong
   for a grid whose whole point is newest first. */
.fye .ppg__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  column-gap: var(--s7);
  row-gap: var(--s7);
  align-items: start;
}
.fye .ppg__grid.is-masonry { grid-auto-rows: 1px; row-gap: 0; }
.fye .ppg__card { min-width: 0; background: var(--white); border: var(--hairline); padding-bottom: var(--s4); align-self: start; }
.fye .ppg__card.is-capped { display: none; }

/* ---- card head ---------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .ppg__head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s3); padding: var(--s3) var(--s4); }
.fye .ppg__mono {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  flex: 0 0 36px;
  width: 36px;
  height: 36px;
  border: var(--hairline);
}
.fye .ppg__mono :where(img) { width: auto; height: 19px; }
.fye .ppg__who { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
.fye .ppg__name { display: block; font-size: var(--fs-small); font-weight: var(--fw-medium); line-height: 1.3; }
.fye .ppg__meta {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* ---- media carousel ----------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .ppg__car { position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-block: var(--hairline); }
.fye .ppg__track { display: flex; transition: transform 420ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
.fye .ppg__slide { position: relative; flex: 0 0 100%; min-width: 0; aspect-ratio: 1; }
.fye .ppg__slide :where(img, video) { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

.fye .ppg__ph { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--ivory); }
.fye .ppg__ph-note { font-size: var(--fs-fine); color: var(--ink-soft); text-align: center; padding: 0 var(--s4); }

.fye .ppg__count,
.fye .ppg__vtag {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 2;
  padding: var(--s1) var(--s2);
  background: var(--scrim);
  color: var(--on-dark);
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  line-height: 1;
}
.fye .ppg__count { top: var(--s3); right: var(--s3); }
.fye .ppg__vtag {
  top: var(--s3);
  left: var(--s3);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s1);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.fye .ppg__vtag .icon { stroke-width: 1.6; }

.fye .ppg__arrow {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  z-index: 3;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 34px;
  height: 34px;
  padding: 0;
  border: var(--hairline);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .ppg__car:hover .ppg__arrow,
.fye .ppg__car:focus-within .ppg__arrow { opacity: 1; }
.fye .ppg__arrow:hover { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .ppg__arrow--prev { left: var(--s3); }
.fye .ppg__arrow--next { right: var(--s3); }

.fye .ppg__dashes { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: var(--s2); padding-top: var(--s4); }
.fye .ppg__dash { width: 16px; height: 2px; background: var(--line); transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease); }
.fye .ppg__dash.is-on { background: var(--line-strong); }

/* ---- words -------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .ppg__caption { padding: var(--s4) var(--s4) 0; font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.68; }
.fye .ppg__caption :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }
.fye .ppg__caption :where(a) { border-bottom: var(--hairline); }
.fye .ppg__spec {
  margin: 0;
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s4) 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  line-height: 1.7;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .ppg__more { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--s10); }

/* ---- reflow: 900 then 560, the theme's own breakpoints ------------------ */
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .ppg__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  /* Touch: there is no hover to reveal an arrow, and 34px is under the 44px
     minimum, so they are always visible and full size here. */
  .fye .ppg__arrow { opacity: 1; width: 44px; height: 44px; }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .ppg__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .fye .ppg__filters { justify-content: flex-start; gap: var(--s2) var(--s5); }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .fye .ppg__track { transition: none; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Past Pieces gallery",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Filters" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_filters", "label": "Show category filters", "default": true,
      "info": "Appears only when pieces span more than one category. Counts fill in automatically."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "all_label", "label": "\"All\" filter label", "default": "All pieces" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "items_initial", "label": "Pieces shown before \"Load more\"", "min": 3, "max": 48, "step": 3, "default": 9 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "more_label", "label": "Load more button label", "default": "Load more pieces" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Background" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "bg_color", "label": "Background", "default": "ivory",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Champagne ivory" },
        { "value": "mist",  "label": "Mist blue" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Advanced" },
    {
      "type": "image_picker", "id": "avatar", "label": "Card monogram",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own monogram."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Past Pieces gallery" }]
}
{% endschema %}
